sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  box rgb(240, 245, 251) User device
    participant B as Browser / React
  end
  box rgb(239, 247, 243) Portal backend
    participant A as Auth Service
    participant R as Redis (sessions)
    participant API as FastAPI backend
    participant D as Download Service
  end
  box rgb(252, 246, 234) Identity provider
    participant I as CTAO IAM
  end
  box rgb(252, 246, 234) Metadata services
    participant T as TAP Server
  end
  box rgb(252, 246, 234) Intermediate DL3 data storage - dCache
    participant S as dCache door / pools
  end
  rect rgb(242, 247, 252)
    Note over B,I: 1. Sign in - OpenID Connect authorization-code flow
    B->>A: Start login
    A-->>B: Set temporary OIDC state cookie, redirect to IAM
    B->>I: Authenticate
    I-->>B: Redirect to callback with code + state
    B->>A: Callback: code + state + temporary OIDC cookie
    A->>A: Validate state
    A->>I: Exchange code + auth-client credentials
    I-->>A: UAT + ID token + optional RT
    A->>A: Validate ID token / nonce
    A->>R: Store session, RT encrypted
    A-->>B: Set HttpOnly SID cookie
    B->>A: GET /auth/me + SID
    A-->>B: Profile, XSRF cookie if missing (no UAT)
    Note over A,R: Still-valid UAT near expiry may be refreshed using RT.<br/>Already-expired UAT requires login again for relay requests.
    Note over A,I: Client secrets remain server-side.
  end
  rect rgb(248, 250, 252)
    Note over B,T: 2. Search and choose an observation
    B->>API: GET /api/search_coords, no user bearer attached
    API->>T: ADQL query on ObsCore table (results may be cached in Redis)
    T-->>API: Observation metadata
    API-->>B: Results
    B->>B: Select primary file reference (LFN / URL)
  end
  rect rgb(242, 247, 252)
    Note over B,S: 3. Prepare and download the file
    B->>A: POST /auth/download/signed-urls + SID
    A->>R: Resolve session and UAT
    R-->>A: Session data
    A->>D: File reference + Bearer UAT (no SID)
    D->>D: Map LFN prefix, check allowed HTTPS host
    D->>I: RFC 8693 exchange: UAT + download-client credentials
    I-->>D: SAT + expiry
    D-->>A: Storage URL + separate SAT + expiry
    A-->>B: Storage descriptor
    Note over B,D: The URL itself is not a signed URL.<br/>Download routes have no explicit CSRF validation.
    B->>S: CORS preflight, HTTPS GET + Bearer SAT
    Note over B,S: Optional door-to-pool redirect follows browser redirect / CORS rules.<br/>Cross-origin Authorization is stripped, SID and UAT are not sent to storage.
    S-->>B: File bytes
    B->>B: Save browser Blob as file
  end
  Note over B,I: SID = session cookie ID, UAT = user access token,<br/>SAT = storage access token, RT = refresh token.
